    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0245" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 180/71 E.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Pierrepont.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President has sent the Vice President of Chile the following telegram:<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d113-f1"/></p>
                <p>You will supplement this by appropriately communicating to the foreign office the
                    condolences of this Government and especially of the Secretary of State.</p>
                <p>The President has directed that the flags on all Government buildings in the
                    District of Columbia be half-masted for three days, which is without precedent
                    at this capital. Messages also have been sent to Mrs. Montt through the embassy
                    at Berlin and the consul at Bremen.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
